# One repo per line: <owner/repo>:<local-folder-name-under-REPOS_DIR>
#
# cp repos.conf.example repos.conf
# then list the repos you want reviewed — any number, not just two.
#
# The left side is the exact "owner/repo" GitHub uses (what `gh search prs`,
# PR URLs, and `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>` all expect). The right side is
# just the folder name your local checkout of it lives in, relative to
# REPOS_DIR (set in config.sh) — it doesn't have to match the GitHub repo
# name, e.g. a repo named "backend" on GitHub checked out locally as "api".
#
# Adding or removing a repo here takes effect on the next poll/click — no
# rebuild, no restart.

cioplenu/backend:api
cioplenu/frontend:frontend
